  "result": "The file is `src/lib/rate-limit.ts`. It holds both pieces:\n\n- **The declaration:** `RATE_LIMIT_BUCKETS` sets the allowance per action. The `\"auth:password-reset\"` bucket has `capacity: 5` and `refillPerMinute: 1`. `DEFAULT_BUCKET` covers any key not in the table.\n- **The decision:** `consumeRateLimit()` refills the bucket for elapsed time, then sets `allowed = tokens >= cost`. When the bucket is empty, `allowed` is false and the verdict carries a `resetAt` time, which is the \"come back later\" signal.\n\nThe password-reset action in `src/actions/auth/reset-password.ts` only calls `consumeRateLimit(ANONYMOUS_ORG_ID, RESET_BUCKET)` and throws `RateLimitedError` when the verdict is not allowed. It does not declare the limit itself, so it is not part of the answer.\n\nANSWER: src/lib/rate-limit.ts",
